{"format":"markdown","content":"FlockWatch is a passive RF detector designed for wearable M5StickC Plus 2 hardware (specifically the Watch Kit so it can be worn on the wrist, but this isn't required). It passively listens to public Wi-Fi management broadcasts and BLE advertisements emitted by surveillance hardware, such as ALPRs (Automated License Plate Readers) and acoustic gunshot detection sensors, to help map public surveillance infrastructure (including Flock Safety ALPRs, among others).

This project is built natively in C++ using PlatformIO and comes with a desktop companion client app written in python.

This is in beta, so submit any bugs you find to GitHub."}

{"format":"markdown","content":"**A guitar chord navigator firmware for the M5Stack Cardputer family** (Cardputer ADV / original Cardputer). Built with PlatformIO + the Arduino framework.

Pick or type a chord and get playable fingerings — or go the other way and identify a chord from a fingering. Voicings aren't looked up from a fixed dictionary: they're **generated algorithmically from the current tuning**, so every feature works the same way with any tuning preset, a custom per-string tuning, a capo, 7-string guitars, and 4/5-string basses.

This is built through "vibe coding" — I describe ideas to Claude and it does the coding."}

