{"format":"markdown","content":"** Latest version from GitHub. Tested and working on Fire v2.7 (Should also work on OG Core) **

WiFi Hash Purple Monster, store EAPOL & PMKID packets to an SD CARD using a M5STACK / ESP32 device.

90% of the code is based on the great PacketMonitor32 from @spacehuhn and the port to M5Stack from macsbug. This firmware mimics the operation of @pwnagotchi in an ESP32 SoC."}

{"format":"markdown","content":"KProx turns an M5Stack Cardputer into a one-button programmable BLE + USB keyboard, boot protocol/HID boot interface and mouse. No software required on the target. Control it via a web interface or REST API over WiFi. Automation sequences are written in a built-in DSL or KProx Script. Credentials are stored in an on-device KeePass KDBX 3.1 database and injected during playback. KProx features menagerie of "apps" such as an IRC client, Nostr Client, TOTP manager and more.

Quick start: https://github.com/akoerner/kprox/blob/master/quick_start.md 

Source: https://github.com/akoerner/kprox"}

{"format":"markdown","content":"A cosmos in your palm — stars dance, trails fade, the universe breathes. But listen. In the deep silence of the night, when the room is dark and your eyes have grown accustomed to the drifting constellations, a faint signal emerges from the tiny speaker. A warning, crossing light-years. You thought you were watching chaos. But chaos was watching you.

掌中宇宙，星移斗转，尾迹如烟。 但且静听。 夜深人静之时，灯熄室暗之后，当你的目光已随星云飘荡许久—— 那微弱的扬声器里，传来一个信号。 跨越光年的警告。 你以为你在欣赏混沌。 但混沌，也在注视着你。（有彩蛋哦）

H for Help"}

